A||||5||HummelHund||Stumbling and Stalling 2.5L||||11||
Z||000000||HummelHund||04-21-2001||08:27 PM||||Although I still haven't fixed my idling problem completely (keeps giving me MAP sensor codes despite having replaced the MAP sensor and its vaccuum hose), a new problem has reared its ugly head. When my car finally started idling normally (takes about 5 min.) I decided to take it for a spin around the block. I noticed that it stumbled under acceleration, and then, while on a slight incline, it died, then almost wouldn't restart, I had to give it some gas to get it going again. I would suspect that this problem is fuel related because of that, but what should I look at first? I've already replaced the fuel filter as part of a complete tune-up I gave it. It gave me no codes, what could be wrong? Injector, relay, fuel pump (God forbid)? Any suggestions would be greatly appreciated, I want to get my baby in driving condition.<P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||04-21-2001||08:40 PM||||check for vac leaks. (Read around in my cave for places to start <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A> )<P>New MAP may be bad or connected to wrong place on motor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rex||04-21-2001||08:42 PM||||Lets not rule out "bad gas". Add some gas treatment to the tank. Give it the fuel treatment/injector cleaner and give it one more spin around the block.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HummelHund||04-21-2001||09:32 PM||||I'll try some injector cleaner first, since it's the cheapest. Which brand should I use? They're all about the same price, so what has everyone had the best luck with?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rex||04-21-2001||09:47 PM||||I've had good results with several brands. Make sure to read the bottle and make sure it has a water displacer. Sounds like you may have moisture in your gas||||reg||1
Z||000005||HummelHund||04-22-2001||05:19 PM||||Ok, I put some Gumout Fuel Treatment and some Water Displacer in the tank. I let it sit about 30 min. and then drove it around the block. Still stumbles. Should I let it sit overnight and try again tomorrow? Do these things take time? What should I try next? I did the leaking injector test from the Haynes manual (unplug injector connector, turn car to ON position, watch for leaks) but saw no leaks. Is there anything else I can test to find what's wrong with my Fiero?<P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
